When you first connect your Mac to Wi-Fi and want to reach your router (192.168.1.1):

Your Mac knows the router's IP address is 192.168.1.1, but it does not know the router's physical hardware MAC address yet.

Your Mac cannot whisper directly to the router because it doesn't know where it physically is on the Wi-Fi.

Your Mac sends an ARP request to the Broadcast Address (192.168.1.255):

"Megaphone Shout: Who has IP 192.168.1.1? Tell 192.168.1.8 your hardware address!"

Every phone, TV, and laptop on your Wi-Fi hears the message, sees it isn't meant for them, and ignores it.

The Airtel router hears it and replies: "That's me! Here is my hardware address."
